//! The intrinsic names LangRef documents.
//!
//! Generated by `corpus/intrinsic-names.nu`, which explains the derivation.
//! In short: upstream builds a declaration from the call for an `llvm.*` name
//! it recognises and reports "use of undefined value" for one it does not,
//! so telling those apart needs the set of real names, and the only
//! specification of that set this project may read is LangRef.
//!
//! The list is deliberately incomplete: it has what LangRef documents and not
//! the target-specific intrinsics that live in each backend's own tables, so
//! `llvm.amdgcn.ds.append` is still refused when undeclared. That is a gap
//! with a number attached rather than a guess.

/// Whether LangRef documents this base name.
pub fn is_documented(base: &str) -> bool {
    NAMES.binary_search(&base).is_ok()
}

